    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "\"The purpose of this report is to make available in digital form the computer spreadsheets that were created for an assessment of in-place gas resources in low-permeability Upper Cretaceous and lower Tertiary sandstone reservoirs, Wind River Basin, Wyoming (Johnson and others, 1996). These spreadsheets are the digital equivalent of the tables released in OF 96-264, with a brief explanation. However, the play spreadsheets include an additional panel, panel 4, that presents an example of the volume of gas that would be recoverable at a given recovery factor. Because the 23 spreadsheets required two 3.5 inch diskettes, it is necessary to transfer all of the spreadsheets from both diskettes into a single folder before opening the aggregation spreadsheet called WR-agg. The reason for this precaution is that the WR-agg spreadsheet is linked to the 22 play spreadsheets. The computer and software requirements are the following: IBM-PC compatible computer with at least 4 Mbyte of hard disk storage available; Windows 95, Microsoft Word 7.0 for Windows 95, and Microsoft Excel 7.0 for Windows 95; or compatible versions.\"",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
